"relationship": "related_topic",
"comparison": "While Citi details specific liquidity agreements and APAs for its conduits, Bank of America discusses the accounting treatment for certain short-term borrowings, primarily short-term structured liabilities, under the fair value option. Citi's disclosure is operational regarding the mechanics of liquidity support (APAs and lending commitments) for conduits, whereas Bank of America's disclosure is financial reporting oriented, focusing on why the fair value option is elected for specific debt instruments due to risk management practices. Both deal with short-term funding instruments, but Citi's focus is on the liquidity facility structure for conduits, while Bank of America's focus is on the valuation method for structured liabilities.",
