"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both Citi and Morgan Stanley provide liquidity facilities to support short-term securities issued by conduits or trusts. Citi provides liquidity agreements to its Citi-Administered Asset-Backed Commercial Paper Conduits to fund them in the event of market disruption. Similarly, Morgan Stanley supports short-term securities (specifically Municipal Tender Option Bonds) with liquidity facilities that allow investors to put their interests, provided by either a third party or the Firm. Both disclosures confirm the bank's role in providing this liquidity backstop to maintain the liquidity of the short-term instruments.",
